# Dynamic element conversion rejects an incompatible stored subtype

Verifies a conversion whose stored subtype has no registered conversion to the
target reports a clean diagnostic naming the value's complete type and the
declared target instead of silently converting.

>>> source
let sizes: int[] = [10mm, 5kg]
let index = 1
print(sizes[index]->to(mm))

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: conversion from `int64[kg]` to `->to(mm)` is not defined

<<< exit
1
